%S A399880 0,1,1,0,20,1,1,3,0,1,1,1,156,1,1,0,272,1,1,20,204,1,1,1,0,1,3,1,812,
%T A399880 1,1,15,544,1,1,0,1332,1,1,1,1640,1,1,1,20,1,1,1,0,1,1,156,2756,1,1,1,
%U A399880 1704,1,1,1,3660,1,1,0,2944,1,1,272,2524,1,1,1,5256,1,1
%N A399880 On Artin's conjecture, (a(n)/A399881(n))*C is the relative density of primes with primitive root n among the primes, where C = A005596 is Artin's constant.
%H A399880 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399880/b399880.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A399880 Oleksiy Klurman, Igor E. Shparlinski, and Joni Teräväinen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1112/blms.70103">On Artin's conjecture on average and short character sums</a>. Bull. London Math. Soc., 57 (2025): 2429-2443.
%H A399880 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399880/a399880_1.txt">Artin(n) for n = 1..10000</a>.
%H A399880 Jianing Song, <a href="/A399880/a399880.txt">PARI code for Artin()</a>.
%H A399880 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ArtinsConstant.html">Artin's constant</a>.
%H A399880 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artin%27s_conjecture_on_primitive_roots">Artin's conjecture on primitive roots</a>.
%H A399880 <a href="/index/Ar#Artin">Index entries for sequences related to Artin's conjecture</a>
%F A399880 Let Artin(n)*C be the relative density of primes with primitive root n among the primes. For |n|>1, write n = (b^2*c)^k where b^2*c is not a prime power and c is squarefree. Artin's conjecture gives:
%F A399880 (i) If c == 2, 3 (mod 4), then Artin(n) = Product_{q|k prime} q*(q-2)/(q^2-q-1);
%F A399880 (ii) If c == 1 (mod 4), set
%F A399880   S := {p prime : p divides c, p does not divide k}, T := {q prime: q divides c, q divides k}, U := {q prime : q does not divide c, q divides k},
%F A399880 then Artin(n) = (((Product_{p in S} p^2-p-1)*(Product_{q in T} q*(q-2)) - (Product_{p in S} -1)*(Product_{q in T} -q)) / ((Product_{p in S} p^2-p-1)*(Product_{q in T} q^2-q-1))) * (Product_{q in U} q*(q-2)/(q^2-q-1)).
%F A399880 The formula is given in the Klurman, Shparlinski, and Teräväinen link.
%e A399880 Let n = 21 (c = 21, b = 1). Then:
%e A399880 - For k = 1, i.e., S = {3,7}, T empty, we have Artin(21) = (5 * 41 - (-1) * (-1))/(5 * 41) = 204/205;
%e A399880 - For k = 3, i.e., S = {7}, T = {3}, we have Artin(21^3) = (41 * 3 - (-1) * (-3))/(5 * 41) = 24/41;
%e A399880 - For k = 7, i.e., S = {3}, T = {7}, we have Artin(21^7) = (5 * 35 - (-1) * (-7))/(5 * 41) = 168/205;
%e A399880 - For k = 21, i.e., S empty, T = {3,7}, we have Artin(21^21) = (3 * 35 - (-3) * (-7))/(5 * 41) = 84/205.
%o A399880 (PARI) A399880(n) = numerator(Artin(n)) \\ See Links for Artin()
%Y A399880 Cf. A005596, A399881 (denominator), A399882/A399883 ({Artin(-n)}).
%K A399880 nonn,frac,new
